                        ],
                        "form": "бди́тельности"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "9d9e4c7e-3938-4fbd-b16e-17407106e0cf",
                        "entry_id": "e2afef12-f80f-3e8b-9cc9-c71b20e5e6d3",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "бди́тельностях"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "051f02e5-fd5f-3c70-aca0-b009f876bb96",
                        "entry_id": "e2afef12-f80f-3e8b-9cc9-c71b20e5e6d3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "свойство по значению прилагательного бдительный; неослабное внимание"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7ab9caab-3091-474f-8a04-1e748ec87610",
                                "sense_id": "051f02e5-fd5f-3c70-aca0-b009f876bb96",
                                "text": "Усыпить чью-нибудь бдительность."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4b65b075-8ce9-4484-9aea-7ba928680fa5",
                                "sense_id": "051f02e5-fd5f-3c70-aca0-b009f876bb96",
                                "text": "В безмолвии должно иметь смирение, и при попечениях бдительность над собою, и удерживать свой помысл."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c3a9baad-a120-4586-b08a-3ba616a60c3b",
                                "sense_id": "051f02e5-fd5f-3c70-aca0-b009f876bb96",
                                "text": "Сияющие, как у всех землян, сказочные зелёные очи жительницы Земли под внешней ласковостью таили непоколебимую отвагу и бдительность, стояли на страже её внутреннего мира."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cb6d0876-f8e4-4742-ab69-f709de8f3966",
                        "source_entry_id": "e2afef12-f80f-3e8b-9cc9-c71b20e5e6d3",
                        "source_sense_id": "051f02e5-fd5f-3c70-aca0-b009f876bb96",
                        "target_lang_word": "vigilance",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "vigilance",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d62dd00d-9f0f-3b41-a046-f52ce3983788",
                                        "entry_id": "83a5ef6f-b28b-304b-a67a-7ed2fb908674",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alert watchfulness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0cfedda3-6acc-400b-ab36-9e1d8fb950db",
                                                "sense_id": "d62dd00d-9f0f-3b41-a046-f52ce3983788",
                                                "text": "To-night she took her accustomed place; for, during the night, no vigilance could satisfy her but her own: any eye but hers might close in momentary forgetfulness."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e526e4b4-4f70-494e-84fe-60242281db79",
                                                "sense_id": "d62dd00d-9f0f-3b41-a046-f52ce3983788",
                                                "text": "I corralled the judge, and we started off across the fields, in no very mild state of fear of that gentleman's wife, whose vigilance was seldom relaxed. And thus we came by a circuitous route to Mohair, the judge occupied by his own guilty thoughts, and I by others not less disturbing."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f735780b-06c8-3654-831b-1b3c3049b409",
                                        "entry_id": "83a5ef6f-b28b-304b-a67a-7ed2fb908674",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Close and continuous attention."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0ca4bbfc-450d-4d33-92fe-1c4dc9d325d1",
                                                "sense_id": "f735780b-06c8-3654-831b-1b3c3049b409",
                                                "text": "But you must remember, my fellow-citizens, that eternal vigilance by the people is the price of liberty, and that you must pay the price if you wish to secure the blessing."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "95656442-fa03-3303-a6e4-4cb55bc19dc0",
                                        "entry_id": "83a5ef6f-b28b-304b-a67a-7ed2fb908674",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A guard; a person set to watch."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "21ca3f4d-8f5b-4027-b0f0-e876da939467",
                        "source_entry_id": "e2afef12-f80f-3e8b-9cc9-c71b20e5e6d3",
                        "source_sense_id": "051f02e5-fd5f-3c70-aca0-b009f876bb96",
                        "target_lang_word": "watchfulness",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "watchfulness",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ce07ae8d-8174-3915-bd32-5dcb068d4620",
                                        "entry_id": "b5a3c981-3a18-32a6-b64d-882a528d7b62",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state or quality of being watchful; alertness, vigilance or wakefulness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b2ecd44-da6a-4d86-a326-cc0f4fda3aba",
                                                "sense_id": "ce07ae8d-8174-3915-bd32-5dcb068d4620",
                                                "text": "Continuous watchfulness is maintained around the clock."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a2545ad7-97d3-476c-a61c-8603a1bfd96e",
                                                "sense_id": "ce07ae8d-8174-3915-bd32-5dcb068d4620",
                                                "text": "The first thing to be undertaken in this weighty work, is a watchfulness over the failings and an inlargement of the dominion, of the Senses."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "16d3e218-335d-491c-8316-39e63800bd37",
                                                "sense_id": "ce07ae8d-8174-3915-bd32-5dcb068d4620",
                                                "text": "1784, Samuel Johnson, letter addressed to Mr. Langton dated 25 August, 1784, cited in James Boswell, The Life of Samuel Johnson, London: Charles Dilly, 1791, Volume 2, p. 545,\nNights of watchfulness produce torpid days […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e93076aa-20cf-4d99-b908-544330b0151c",
                                                "sense_id": "ce07ae8d-8174-3915-bd32-5dcb068d4620",
                                                "text": "Every dark form in the dimness had its ominous quality, its peculiar suggestion of alert watchfulness."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "93c7ce21-a023-4e77-b160-bbefeb92c717",
                                                "sense_id": "ce07ae8d-8174-3915-bd32-5dcb068d4620",
                                                "text": "The steady rhythm of the engines, the fact that he had been sleeping badly, the boredom of a flight that he had done so many times before and did not want to do again, the long humiliation and unhappiness that was always in the background of his mind, all fought against his watchfulness."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "062f820c-c405-416c-8a34-272da248eb7b",
                        "source_entry_id": "e2afef12-f80f-3e8b-9cc9-c71b20e5e6d3",
